# THE SAME SYSTEM SAID A DIFFERENT WAY. One row per relabelling: what it rewrites, the
# sentence in the schema that says a rule must not notice, and whether the model claims the
# verdicts hold still.
#
# ⭐⭐⭐ A COVERING WORD IS A CLAIM ABOUT WHAT THE RULES CANNOT SEE, AND NOTHING HERE TESTED IT.
#    `HolderKind` says "unserved" and not "refused", and argues the choice: both of the other
#    two name an ACTOR, a card that errors a request did refuse it, a caller who waits past
#    their patience was refused by nobody. Then the load-bearing sentence: BOTH LAND IN THE
#    SAME TWO HOLDERS, SO THE WORD COVERING THEM MUST NOT DECIDE WHICH HAPPENED. That is a
#    falsifiable statement about every rule in checks/, and it was asserted in prose and
#    checked by nothing -- the same condition the whole checks/ tree exists to end.
#
# ⭐⭐ THE TEST IS A REWRITE, NOT A NEW FILING. Say the shortfall twice, once as a refusal and
#    once as a decay, holding the demand, the nameplate, the remainder, the fit, the holders
#    and every magnitude fixed. If a rule returns a different verdict on the two, the rule
#    decided which happened, and the covering word has a counter-example.
#
# ⛔⛔ THE THIRD ROW IS THE DEFEATER AND IT IS NOT OPTIONAL. Two relabellings expected to hold
#    still are two ways of learning nothing, because a harness that compares a relation to
#    itself reports `steady` for every input including a broken one. `unserved_as_absorbed`
#    crosses a line the rules DO read, so it MUST move; the day it does not, the diff is
#    wrong and the other two rows are worth nothing. Same argument as the three deliberate
#    defects the validator was made to reject before any pass was believed.
#
# ⛔ `expected` IS THE GATE AND `swaps` IS THE PARAMETER. The rewrites live in
#   assets/sql/invariance.sql as statements, because a perturbation is not a relation; what
#   each one is FOR is here, where it can be read without running anything.
-- pm:HolderKind, the "unserved" annotation; pm:Layer/pm:timeSlack, "the holder does not get to refuse".
SELECT * FROM (VALUES
  ('refusal_as_decay',
   'capacity slack <-> time slack, on a layer whose shortfall nobody could serve',
   'the same demand went without because the supply had no room to run into, or because it did not survive the wait',
   'steady'),
  ('experienced_or_not',
   'customer <-> unrealised, where a layer names only one of the two',
   'demand that was there and got degraded, or demand that never became anybody''s experience',
   'steady'),
  ('unserved_as_absorbed',
   'customer -> people, where a layer has no people holder already',
   'THE DEFEATER: this one crosses unserved into absorbed, which the rules read on purpose',
   'moves')
) AS t(slug, swaps, tests, expected)
